From 4891e4cb1e448956cd1b3d4a704dd96a3cfe4542 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleg Tolmatcev <oleg.tolmatcev@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:07:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] fix: ignore break and continue outside a loop, as bash
 does

Outside a loop, `break` and `continue` still returned loop control flow,
which nothing consumed: a script run from a file stopped there with
status 0.  gawk's configure has a stray `break` in its mpfr check
(unspecified in POSIX, a no-op in bash, dash and ksh), so configure
ended early without an error.

Count the loops enclosing the current command, starting again at 0 in
functions and subshells as bash does.  Outside a loop, warn and return
0; `break n` and `continue n` beyond the enclosing loops act on the
outermost one.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
